description:
* Drop missing values in `.x` by default. Fixes #315.
* New `.na_last` argument to control position of NAs. Fixes #266.

@DavisVaughan what do you think of this API? It's a bit unusual to default to `na.rm = TRUE`, but you can't see the result of the computation and including `NA`s is never useful, so adopting ggplot2's approach makes sense to me. Once you've reviewed this API, I'll also apply it to `fct_reorder2()`.

Fix #16 

@hadley, I saw what you meant in the #16 discussion about affecting the value and not just the levels.  That is addressed here.  Also, I removed the `.desc` argument.  Since it was both simpler and potentially friendlier to the user to leave the `decreasing` argument from `base::order()` exposed (it doesn't have the `dplyr` dependency to sort decreasing), I left that.  And, I made the default `method` "radix" so that it would work with a vector of values for `decreasing` (something that would annoy me whenever I forgot that I needed to set the method, and it seemed like a minor wart to add an argument directly).

Anyway, let me know what you think and if I'm missing something else important.
